# File finder exclusions (US-002). One glob per line, gitignore syntax without
# trailing slashes. A bare name matches a file or folder at any depth; a glob
# containing "/" is anchored at the searched home folder unless it starts with
# "**/". The same list drives the name index (fd --exclude) and text search
# (rg --glob '!...'), so an entry here is never indexed, listed, previewed, or
# searched by content.

# Secret stores, matched at any depth so copies inside other homes, backups,
# and agent profiles stay hidden too.
.password-store
.gnupg
.ssh
keyrings
.env
.env.*
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
.netrc
.git-credentials
.pgpass
**/.codex/auth.json
**/.claude/.credentials.json
**/gh/hosts.yml
**/.docker/config.json
**/.kube/config

